Industrial Compression Watch: Hydrogen and IIoT Reshape Equipment Demand
Process gas compression is increasingly influenced by the transition toward lower-carbon energy systems and the digitalization of industrial equipment. Hydrogen projects require compressors capable of handling demanding pressure and purity requirements, creating opportunities for specialized oil-free systems.

Industrial IoT is another major development. Sensors embedded within compressor systems can monitor vibration and temperature and provide data for predictive maintenance. Digital monitoring can help operators identify equipment degradation before failures occur, while remote commissioning and performance analytics are increasingly relevant for complex industrial and offshore projects.

